# Riverglades for the Alliance (2026-11-12, part of the route since 0.4.0: after Stranglethorn Vale, before the
# Badlands & Hinterlands). Hand-written from players'
# recordings of the zone (123 sessions to 2026-11-12) and Forever's quest data (the client's quest records,
# QuestieDB 1.0.16 and EG Link) for titles, levels, objectives and places.
# Order: the way in from Redridge through Blackrock Pass; the western hubs in one pass (Scout Bolain, Southern
# Watch, Turner's Logging Camp, the Bristle Hills, the Holmsby farm and the river, where Benjy Wheeler's murlocs,
# Halligan's murloc heads and Curly are one sweep, then Curly's rescue from the camp); Farholde Keep (flight path,
# inn); Wheeler's Grange; the plains up to Terral's Watch; Farholde Keep again.
# Freshwater Fiends: Benjy offers it before My Kingdom for a Horse (players' recordings: two characters were offered
# it before they took My Kingdom for a Horse).
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings): From Seed to Sprout after Unsavory Plant
# Food; Foal Play after My Kingdom for a Horse; Coyote Huntin' and Wheeler's Fleeing Steeds after Foal Play;
# Rescue Roundup after Wheeler's Fleeing Steeds; Song of the Strider after A Feast for Buzzards; A Few Furs for Friz
# after A Fur Trade; Watcher Cornelius's Rog'mar errands once his first two hunts are handed in. Apple of My Eye
# (Tessa Dawnbright) and Wound Dressings (Brother Lowley) only once Saving Sunnyglade is handed in, and King of the
# Wild Plains (Ombassa) only once Song of the Strider is (quest data; every recorded offer came after them). So
# Farholde Keep gets a stop between Terral's Watch and the port: Ashe's and Brant's Sunnyglade hand-ins, then Tessa's
# chain, whose Stepped Out opens Innkeeper Zizplink's quests in Powderfuse Port.
# Elites, each behind a group choice: Snargl (40), Ombassa (41); the WANTED posters for Ghostmaw and Blademaster
# Kaijo (42) are taken at the end, for part 2's ground.
# Left out on purpose:
# - The Sharpest of Blades (95184): eight Solid Sharpening Stones, a blacksmith's make; 3 of 16 recorded players
#   handed it in.

step Ironforge flight master
  when zone "Dun Morogh"
  zone Ironforge
  tip The Stranglethorn guide leaves Dwarves and Gnomes at their riding trainer in Dun Morogh: ride back west into Ironforge, where the flight to Lakeshire leaves from the gryphon master.
  goto 55.9,47.9 "Ironforge flight master"

step Into the Riverglades
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  tip Fly from Ironforge to Lakeshire in Redridge, then follow the road north out of town and up through Blackrock Pass: it comes down into the western Riverglades by the Bristle Hills.
  fly "Lakeshire"
  zone Redridge Mountains
  goto 44.8,8.9 "Blackrock Pass"
  zone Riverglades
  goto 16.0,68.5 "The western Riverglades"

step Scout Bolain
  tip Scout Bolain waits beside the road east of the pass.
  tip This guide is written for levels 41-45: the route comes here at about 41, after Stranglethorn Vale. The port's second wave and the Western Front's camps in the north are 43-45, with elite Twilight Enforcers (45) on patrol and Overlord Kilgar (46, elite) for groups only: below 41, do Stranglethorn first.
  accept 95147                          -- The Lost Scout

step Southern Watch
  tip Follow the road east to Southern Watch, the Alliance outpost above the river. The gnolls you passed on the way in are Captain Dalton's job: you go back for them after the lumber camp.
  turnin 95147                          -- Cedric Dalton
  accept 94678                          -- Gnoll Infestation
  accept 95148                          -- Southern Watch Gnoll Report: for Demar Brant in Farholde Keep, keep it

step Snargl's Snout
  when group 94679
